        <!-- Section 1: Global Overview -->
        <section id="global-overview">
            <h2>Global Homicide Rate Overview</h2>
            <p>The global trajectory of intentional homicide rates reveals a nuanced picture of long-term change. After a period of relative stability in the 1990s and an uptick in the 2000s, the 2010s marked a notable decline in global homicide rates, with the trend appearing to stabilize in the early 2020s despite data gaps.</p>

            <div class="highlight">
                <strong>Key Finding:</strong> The global mean homicide rate declined from <strong>8.52 per 100,000</strong> in the 2000s to <strong>7.67 per 100,000</strong> in the 2010s—a 10% improvement. However, the 2020s data (based on limited reporting) shows a slight uptick to 7.80, warranting continued monitoring.
            </div>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="globalTrendChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <p>The chart above illustrates the year-by-year evolution of global homicide rates from 1990 to 2023. The shaded area represents the interquartile range (25th to 75th percentile), while the line shows the median rate. Notably, both the mean and median have generally trended downward since the early 2000s, suggesting a genuine global improvement rather than an artifact of changing participation.</p>

            <h3>Decade-by-Decade Summary</h3>
            <table>
